# Test: on a disk-store DUT whose boot record holds the store's configuration
#       lock for longer than OSPF's five second state deadline, an operator's
#       `request ospf graceful-restart` still prepares the planned restart.
# VALIDATES: through the real entry point, the CLI dialing the daemon's SSH
#            server: grPrepare -> prepareRestart -> persistFact
#            (internal/plugins/ospf/gr_restarter.go) writes the restart fact
#            with StatePut under a 5 s deadline, and the daemon's opStatePut
#            (internal/component/plugin/server/dispatch_state.go) takes the
#            store's runtime-state lock only, so the write does not wait
#            behind the boot record's configuration syncs.
# PREVENTS: on a disk another writer saturates, the boot record holds the
#           configuration lock for up to a minute after ze serves; the planned
#           restart failing there with "ospf: persist graceful restart: ...
#           context deadline exceeded" while the fact still lands later, so
#           the durable store says a restart is in flight that was refused.
#
# The command is sent after "Ze running.", which the hub prints after it has
# started the boot record, and the record takes its hold at once; the SSH
# dial and login alone take longer than that. The hold (14 s) outlasts the
# OSPF deadline (5 s), so a fact write that waits for the record fails.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: with the store's single write lock (the store-fix files at
# HEAD before the configuration/runtime split) the answer carries
# "context deadline exceeded" and "prepared" is false.
#
# No cmd= line carries `:timeout=`: a foreground command's timeout replaces
# option=timeout as the budget of the whole test (resolveOrchestratedTimeout,
# internal/test/runner/runner_exec_util.go).

option=storage:value=disk
option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ZE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.
option=env:var=XDG_DATA_HOME:value=.
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass
option=env:var=ze.test.boot.record.hold:value=14s
stdin=init-answers:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
testpass
127.0.0.1
$PORT2
EOF_INIT
tmpfs=running.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT2;
		}
	}
}
ospf {
	router-id 10.0.0.1
	graceful-restart {
		restarter {
			support planned
		}
	}
	areas {
		area 0.0.0.0 { }
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze init:stdin=init-answers:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze start running.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze cli -c "request ospf graceful-restart | json":exit=0
expect=stdout:contains="prepared": true
reject=stdout:contains=deadline exceeded
cmd=stop:seq=4:name=daemon:signal=term
